12304	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s6","entry":{"id":"review-9bd6b848f1f4ef386643217287bea544","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:06:28.618Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed operation inventory satisfies upstream s6 ac1.","evidence":"DEF.md §6.6 ac1 requires supported operations on Jira issues, projects, transitions, comments and assignment to be reachable. The installed inventory includes attachment delete/list, comment visibility, watchers and create-bulk, but the five proposed families omit them. docs/plans/tool-registry.md calls these outside scope without an upstream amendment. Recording an exclusion does not satisfy reachability. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Implement the supported operations required by ac1 or obtain an explicit upstream scope amendment and align the coverage table and tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Every Jira read except auth status returns JSON.","evidence":"The recorded inventory says search --count prints '✓ Number of work items in the search: N'. Installed search --help describes --count as 'Number of work items in the search'. The LLD nevertheless claims every read has JSON and does not specify the deterministic count-text parser needed to produce {op,count}. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Specify count's actual output and deterministic parser, including malformed-output handling and recorded fixtures.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The registry integration point exists and Jira tools are currently absent.","evidence":"registerBuiltinTools calls registerGhTools and then registerSshTools; it has no Jira registration. Searching src/daemon/tools/builtins found no jira_ definitions or acli spawn target. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/index.ts]","action":"Add the Jira import and registration after registerGhTools as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The unchanged buildArgv function is CLI-neutral and directly reusable for acli.","evidence":"buildArgv initializes 'const argv: string[] = [\\'gh\\', ...def.command]'. It also appends gh-style '--json' followed by a comma-separated field list for items/object outputs. Installed acli help defines --json as a boolean. The LLD specifies neither replacing the executable token nor avoiding the incompatible JSON suffix. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Specify the Jira argv adaptation explicitly: replace the executable, use boolean --json, and choose output specifications that avoid gh field-list generation. Preserve existing gh behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Exporting shape unchanged as resultOf provides the promised Jira batch-failure detection.","evidence":"shape's mutation branch unconditionally returns 'success: true' and 'ok: true'; it never parses results, status, totalCount or successCount. The inventory records exit-0 FAILURE bodies, while §6 assigns their detection to resultOf and §2.12 prohibits changing its behavior. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Define a Jira-specific mutation parser, invoked before success shaping or through OutSpec.custom, and specify its handling of complete, partial and malformed results.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Passing paginate provides the finite list bounds promised by the design.","evidence":"Installed search help says '--paginate Fetch all work items'; project list says it fetches 'all pages' and '--limit is ignored'; comment list likewise says '--limit is ignored'. Therefore accepting paginate is incompatible with 'none runs unbounded'. Capture caps and timeouts do not impose a finite record bound. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Choose a finite maximum result count and specify bounded pagination or remove paginate from these tool inputs. Align tests and postconditions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The project-archive approval contract is consistently specified.","evidence":"§2.9 assigns project archive to common, whereas chosen alternative §9.1 assigns it to destructive. executor.ts resolves the class before execution and can run common operations without asking, so these alternatives produce materially different authorization behavior. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Resolve the project-archive class and use it consistently in the contract, op table, approval preview and tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding the Jira families requires no persistent-data rewrite and need not invalidate the existing approval snapshot.","evidence":"The reused builders construct schemas, argv and results in memory; no persistence is involved. approval-class-mapping.test.ts explicitly iterates the 228 existing snapshot entries and states that tools added by later stories are not compared. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Keep existing definitions and snapshot bytes unchanged; retain the proposed compatibility suites.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed shared-contract integration preserves the executor's ownership of approval and result validation.","evidence":"HLD §5.6 gives s6 ownership of Jira schemas and operation classes. executeTool already validates declared inputs, obtains approval, runs the tool and validates result.data. withGhFailureNet only wraps execution exceptions and missing failure kinds. Reusing these surfaces does not require redesigning s2 or s3. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Keep approval exchange and output validation in the existing executor; export aliases without changing gh behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The linked component companion renders consistently with the proposed dependency structure.","evidence":"Inspected the HTML's narrative, Mermaid source and component table. They describe six components and five directed dependencies, including Jira-to-gh reuse and index-to-Jira registration, consistently with §3.3. No browser rendering was obtained, so Mermaid execution, label layout and rendered readability were not verified. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/component-dependency.html, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Render the existing companion and inspect its diagram and labels before claiming visual verification. No ERD is necessary for these module dependencies alone.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"A failed auth probe reliably distinguishes missing sign-in from network failure.","evidence":"§2.2 classifies a command as missing-signin when its auth probe 'fails', and §6 also treats absence of '✓ Authenticated' as signed out, before network classification. A network-failed probe meets both conditions. Existing ghFailureOf requires an authentication pattern in a failed probe and separately checks network patterns, avoiding this blanket inference. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Represent probe failure separately from confirmed signed-out status. Preserve network, timeout and spawn failures from the probe; classify missing-signin only on positive authentication-failure evidence.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing shell primitive supports closed stdin, direct argv execution and detectable capture/termination failures.","evidence":"runShellBytes uses 'shell: false' and stdin 'ignore' when no input is supplied. It returns spawnError, timedOut, aborted, signal, stdoutTruncated and stderrOverflow; timeout and stderr overflow kill the process group. These support the proposed prompt prevention and failure mapping. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Use these actual result field names and decode stdout bytes explicitly in acliExec.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The proposed coverage test proves upstream ac1 reachability.","evidence":"The LLD's coverage test accepts an excluded command whenever it has a reason. DEF s6 ac1 requires supported operations within its named domains to be reachable. Consequently a test can pass while required supported operations remain inaccessible. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Test a required-operation inventory independently of JIRA_COVERAGE, and reject exclusions of required operations unless supported by an approved scope amendment.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Successful mutation response shapes are established sufficiently to validate the proposed parsers.","evidence":"The inventory records nonexistent-key FAILURE batches and several exit-1 errors. The LLD explicitly says successful create, edit, transition, assign, clone, archive and comment-create bodies were not recorded. Proposed fake outputs and an optional future write test cannot establish those actual success shapes. No live mutations were performed during this review. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Obtain authoritative successful-response fixtures or approved sandbox evidence before fixing parser assumptions, and require those fixtures in mutation parser tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"}],"counts":{"high":8,"med":0,"low":6,"unverified":2},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T18:06:28.618Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
433	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s6","entry":{"id":"b7ad9bd9fca24edbb81875738fea9288","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:08:40.384Z","operation":"review","revision":{"number":1,"contentHash":"2460949690689fb2d609d027dc8822a5f19404e7bd02902f55dda1de445b5155"},"outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"reviewed by the daemon: block","data":{"counts":{"high":8,"med":0,"low":6}}}}}
12084	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s6","entry":{"id":"review-5348c28825d0a3028de89dc36f03a308","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:19:10.726Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The five families cover the upstream Jira domains, with explicitly proposed exclusions.","evidence":"DEF s6 ac1–ac6 require named Jira operations, distinguished installation/auth failures, checked results, destructive approval and acli-only execution. The design addresses each and explicitly requests approval for create-bulk and credential/session exclusions. The recorded inventory supports status-name transitions and names transition IDs and transition listing as unsupported. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Retain the exclusions as proposed until explicitly approved; update the inventory's outdated scope sentence that still excludes attachments, watchers and clone.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Registration is additive and the existing approval snapshot permits new tools.","evidence":"registerBuiltinTools calls registerGhTools among unconditional domain registrations. The snapshot test explicitly says: 'Tools that later Stories add are not in the snapshot and are not compared.' Its loops compare old IDs individually rather than asserting the live registry has 228 entries. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Add the Jira registration after registerGhTools; no snapshot modification is required.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The exported gh primitives support the custom-output argv and failure-wrapper reuse.","evidence":"OpDef, OutSpec, GhFamilyTool, argument constructors and schema/rule builders are exported. buildArgv starts with ['gh', ...def.command] and appends JSON field lists only for items/object outputs. withGhFailureNet preserves existing failures and converts thrown exceptions or unclassified failures to rejected. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Use custom outputs and Jira-owned execution as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The unchanged schema builder can enforce the specified maximum limits and 50-distinct-key cap.","evidence":"FieldSpec has minimum but no maximum or maxItems. fieldSchema emits 'Type.Integer({ minimum: spec.minimum ?? 1, ...d })' and string arrays with only minItems: 1. Neither buildInputSchema nor buildArgv deduplicates keys. Thus the promised schema rejection and duplicate handling do not follow from the selected unchanged builder. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Specify Jira-owned schema augmentation and normalization, including whether deduplication precedes distinct-key validation; enforce each maximum before spawning without modifying gh.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"refuseInput supplies the promised rejection of every leading-dash positional or flag value.","evidence":"refuseInput scans arguments only when opts.dashSafe === true and selects names only from 'pos' or 'spread'. It does not inspect val, csv or rep flag values. buildArgv passes these values through. The design promises 'A positional or a value that starts with ... was refused earlier' but specifies no Jira validation closing this gap. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Define Jira-owned validation for all relevant scalar and array values and explicitly enable positional checking; test flag-valued keys as well as positionals.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Every list can pass the finite --limit promised by defineJiraFamily.","evidence":"The inventory's bounds section identifies --limit for search, project list and comment list. Its recorded attachment and watcher invocations are 'attachment list --key K --json' and 'list-watchers --key K --json'; the design exposes no limit for these, link list or link types, while promising 'Every list passes a finite --limit'. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Limit that invariant to commands supporting pagination controls; document server-bounded reads and capture-cap handling separately.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No stored-record migration is needed for the proposed additive tool registration.","evidence":"The design introduces runtime op tables and output schemas rather than persistent entities. registerBuiltinTools aggregates domain registrations, and callTool delegates to executeTool; neither requires a stored tool-record migration. Existing tool IDs and their schemas are expressly preserved. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Keep the change additive and leave the existing approval snapshot intact.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design consumes shared execution and approval contracts without redesigning their ownership.","evidence":"executeTool validates input, resolves approval, denies unanswered requests before execution, validates successful result data and then runs hooks. shouldAsk returns true unconditionally for destructive. Jira's proposed approval function and declared schemas fit those existing seams; hook registration and caller cutover remain outside this Story. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md]","action":"Exercise Jira calls through executeTool in integration tests so the existing approval and schema checks are included.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The component companion documents the proposed dependency direction consistently with the design.","evidence":"The HTML source declares four components and three arrows from jira to gh/op-table, gh/helpers and shell-helper, with the narrative 'nothing in gh depends on jira'. The component table names the reused exports and Jira ownership. This is sufficient dependency documentation; no persisted entity relationship is introduced. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/component-dependency.html]","action":"Retain the component documentation; an ERD is unnecessary for this change.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.3","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The linked companion renders correctly.","evidence":"Inspected the HTML, embedded Mermaid flowchart, initialization and rendering-error handler. No browser rendering was performed in this read-only review, so layout, labels and successful SVG generation remain unverified. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/component-dependency.html]","action":"Render the existing HTML and verify readable labels, arrow direction and absence of the 'Diagram could not be drawn' fallback.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Closed stdin, timeout and capture-cap outcomes can be implemented using runShellBytes.","evidence":"runShellBytes spawns with 'stdio: [hasStdin ? ... : ignore, ...]' and shell:false, records spawn errors, timeout, abort and signal, marks stdoutTruncated, and kills on stderr overflow. The inventory independently records cancelled prompts with closed stdin and FAILURE batches at exit 0. The proposed Jira readers address that exit-0 failure case. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Preserve these outcome fields and reject truncated output before parsing.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Unrecognized visibility output is always rejected rather than returned as an empty list.","evidence":"readVisibility specifies undefined when the heading is missing, but provides no distinction between an explicitly empty result and an unrecognized or malformed body beneath a valid heading. The recorded group form includes '(N total)' and a box table; the role form uses '- Name' lines. A heading-only or changed-format answer could therefore satisfy the stated reader contract while silently losing rows. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Specify body validation and explicit empty-result evidence, including group count consistency; reject malformed rows or nonempty unrecognized bodies.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each upstream acceptance criterion has a named planned proving test.","evidence":"Compared DEF s6 ac1–ac6 with §7: coverage/family tests address ac1; failure and credential tests ac2; schemas/parsers ac3; approval tests ac4; spawn-only tests ac5; unsupported-operation coverage ac6. These are planned tests, not verified implementation results. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Retain the mapping and include executor-level approval denial tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The planned live test closes the acknowledged evidence gap for project mutation success readers.","evidence":"The open question says project create, update and restore success text was not probed and 'the live test should record the real text'. However, the live subjects cover read operations and work-item create/delete with clone cleanup; no project mutation is included. The inventory likewise records no successful project mutation output. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Add an explicitly gated disposable-project probe for those readers, or provide captured authoritative output and a concrete verification gate before claiming support.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":3,"low":9,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T18:19:10.726Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
