11307	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s6","entry":{"id":"review-933226956f2a8dd79a041650380d06d3","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:26:45.531Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The five families cover the upstream Jira domains, subject to explicit approval of the proposed exclusions.","evidence":"DEF §6.6 requires operations on issues, projects, transitions, comments and assignment, plus named unsupported operations. The design addresses these domains and explicitly proposes excluding create-bulk and session-changing commands. These exclusions remain proposed amendments, not already approved scope. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Record the exclusion amendment when the user approves; fix the project-create contract identified below before approval.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The gh builder lacks maximum, maxItems and deduplication, and its optional dash check covers positionals rather than flag values.","evidence":"fieldSchema emits integer minimum and array minItems: 1. buildArgv preserves array members. refuseInput selects only 'pos' and 'spread' when dashSafe is true; flag values are not inspected there. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Retain Jira-owned bounds, normalization and identifier validation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"There is no existing Jira tool implementation, and the approval snapshot permits additional tools.","evidence":"Production src matches for Jira are the provider-source declarations in shared/understanding.ts and understanding/identity.ts. registerBuiltinTools has no Jira registration. approval-class-mapping.test.ts explicitly says tools added by later Stories 'are not in the snapshot and are not compared' and iterates snapshot entries rather than requiring registry size equality. [files: src/shared/understanding.ts, src/understanding/identity.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Use the proposed additive registration.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The exported gh builder and failure net can support custom Jira execution without editing gh files.","evidence":"op-table.ts exports OpDef, OutSpec, argument constructors, refuseInput, buildArgv, buildInputSchema, buildOutputSchema, rejectInput and GhFamilyTool. Custom outputs supply shape and build. withGhFailureNet wraps execute, preserves existing failures and converts exceptions to rejected failures; it does not spawn gh. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Reuse these exports with the Jira executor and custom output builders.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The specified jira_project create inputs are sufficient to invoke the installed acli project-create command.","evidence":"LLD §2.17 supplies key, name and optional project details but no source project or JSON definition. Installed `acli jira project create --help` describes creation 'from an existing project', shows `--from-project \"TEAM\" --key \"NEWTEAM\" --name \"New Project\"`, and offers `--from-project` or `--from-json`. The proposed contract exposes neither creation source, so its documented create call is incomplete. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Add and validate a source-project input mapped to --from-project, document its company-managed-project restriction, and update argv tests and disposable-project probe prerequisites.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Returning GhFamilyTool preserves concrete per-family input and output types for callTool callers.","evidence":"The proposed defineJiraFamily returns GhFamilyTool. That alias is `TypedTool & { readonly ops: readonly OpDef[] }`; TypedTool declares inputSchema and outputSchema only as TSchema, and both schema builders return TSchema. callTool derives its types with Static<T['inputSchema']> and Static<T['outputSchema']>. Concrete Jira fields and discriminated output members are therefore erased by the declared return type. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Specify concrete family schema types or another type-preserving factory contract, and add compile-time checks that invalid inputs and invalid output-property access fail.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The change can be additive without rewriting stored records or changing existing tool contracts.","evidence":"The registry stores tools by id in an in-memory Map. Builtins are explicitly registered by domain. The proposed new ids do not replace existing registrations, and no persistent Jira records or storage schema changes are introduced. The custom output builder uses Type.Object without additionalProperties:false, permitting additional REST properties when known fields satisfy their declared types. [files: src/daemon/tools/registry.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Keep the existing-schema snapshot checks and ensure optional nullable REST fields are represented as unknown or explicitly nullable.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design consumes the shared executor and approval contracts without redesigning their ownership.","evidence":"executeTool validates typed-tool input before approval, resolves the per-input class, denies unanswered approval, validates successful result data and then runs hooks. approval-policy.ts always asks for destructive operations. The design assigns Jira classes and readers while leaving these shared stages intact. Its prose and companion source identify the one-way Jira dependencies and their responsibilities; no persistent entity relationship or UI change requires an ERD or UX mock. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/component-dependency.html]","action":"Retain the shared executor path and Jira-owned adapter boundary.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The generated component companion renders consistently with its source.","evidence":"Inspected the generated HTML narrative, Mermaid source, component table and rendering initialization. They describe four components and three Jira dependency arrows consistently with the LLD. Attempting to open the file through the browser tool failed with 'Browser is not available: iab'; no rendered diagram was observed. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/component-dependency.html]","action":"Render the existing companion and inspect labels, arrows and layout before claiming visual verification.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The planned failure handling addresses exit-zero batch failures, incomplete capture, timeouts and ambiguous authentication failures.","evidence":"The recorded acli probes show exit-zero FAILURE results and clone ids containing the source key. runShellBytes exposes timedOut, aborted, signal, stdoutTruncated and stderrOverflow, closes stdin when none is supplied, and kills on stderr overflow. The design explicitly checks batch status/counts, rejects incomplete output and requires positive authentication-probe evidence. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts]","action":"Implement the stated precedence and test both complete and partial batch failures.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Project mutation success readers are grounded in recorded successful acli output.","evidence":"The repository inventory records successful work-item, comment and link mutations, but not successful project create, update, archive, restore or delete. The LLD explicitly acknowledges that these texts are unknown. Local --help confirms command flags, not success-output formatting; no project mutation was performed during this review. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Complete the gated disposable-project probe after correcting its creation inputs, preserve fixtures and validate all five readers before accepting them.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream s6 acceptance criterion has a corresponding planned behavioral test.","evidence":"Compared DEF §6.6 ac1–ac6 with the acceptance mapping: coverage and family execution address ac1; missing-tool/sign-in and credential checks address ac2; schemas and parsers address ac3; destructive classes and no-client denial address ac4; spawn-only tests address ac5; unsupported-operation checks address ac6. The tests are proposed, so this establishes mapping rather than passing implementation evidence. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/__tests__/_fakegh.ts]","action":"Retain this mapping, add the project-create source-input cases and compile-time typing checks identified above, and require recorded project fixtures rather than treating a skipped live probe as validation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":0,"low":10,"unverified":2},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T18:26:45.531Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
434	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s6","entry":{"id":"b75a20d16ecb4d5a9941877c99afc319","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:29:39.351Z","operation":"review","revision":{"number":3,"contentHash":"7b40641f0b685ffac342fd78cd68c7ec82cc03e2f61d40cd486b5ff0c6561ab7"},"outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"reviewed by the daemon: block","data":{"counts":{"high":2,"med":0,"low":10}}}}}
9618	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s6","entry":{"id":"review-2bea578c3e63c29eef75c84cd05a7fd4","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:35:32.211Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The operation coverage satisfies upstream ac1 without changing its scope.","evidence":"DEF s6 ac1 requires an operation that acli supports on issues and projects to be reachable. The recorded inventory includes workitem create-bulk and project JSON forms, which this design deliberately excludes. The design acknowledges that approval must authorize a scope amendment; these exclusions do not yet satisfy the unchanged criterion. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Record the proposed exclusions as an explicit amendment to ac1 and obtain its approval with the LLD.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The gh builder lacks maximum, maxItems and deduplication, checks leading dashes only on positionals, and returns broadly typed schemas.","evidence":"Read fieldSchema, refuseInput, buildArgv, buildInputSchema and GhFamilyTool. Arrays have minItems: 1; integers have minimum only. The dash loop selects only pos/spread arguments. GhFamilyTool is 'TypedTool & { readonly ops: readonly OpDef[] }'. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts]","action":"Retain the Jira-owned bounds, normalization and flag-value checks.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Recorded acli behavior supports deterministic readers and checking batch results despite exit zero.","evidence":"The approved write probe records exit-zero FAILURE batches, clone ids containing the source key, count text, visibility formats, and transitions:null. Installed search and unarchive help also confirm the proposed selection, JSON and confirmation flags. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Use these recorded cases as fixtures.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Jira can reuse the named exported builder functions and failure wrapper without changing gh files.","evidence":"The named types, argument constructors, schema builders, refuseInput and rejectInput are exported. buildArgv starts with ['gh', ...def.command] and appends JSON fields only for items/object outputs. withGhFailureNet wraps execution independently of the CLI command. Source search found no existing Jira tool implementation. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/index.ts]","action":"Retain the custom-output adapter and Jira-owned execution path.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding registration after registerGhTools is sufficient to expose the five new builtins without updating the approval snapshot.","evidence":"registerBuiltinTools calls each domain unconditionally; daemon/index.ts calls that aggregator. The snapshot test explicitly says new tools 'are not in the snapshot and are not compared' and iterates existing snapshot entries. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/index.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts]","action":"Add the import and registration call plus the proposed five-id registration test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The linked component companion renders consistently with the documented dependency direction.","evidence":"Inspected the HTML Mermaid source: jira points to gh/op-table, gh/helpers and shell-helper, matching §3.4. The generated HTML and embedded renderer exist. No local Chromium executable was available; browser rendering and visual layout were not verified. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/component-dependency.html]","action":"Render the existing companion and check labels, arrows and layout. The prose already adequately documents ownership and compatibility; no ERD is necessary for these module dependencies.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed tools require no migration of stored records or existing tool contracts.","evidence":"The existing aggregator has no Jira registration. The inspected Tool/callTool/executor path operates on tool definitions and results; the design adds new ids and transient schemas without introducing persistent storage or changing existing definitions. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Retain additive registration and verify existing ids and schemas remain unchanged.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Deferring concrete family types fully preserves the shared sc2 contract.","evidence":"HLD sc2 promises 'a result typed from the tool definition they pass'. callTool derives Static<T['outputSchema']>, but GhFamilyTool widens both schemas to TSchema. The design correctly admits concrete caller types are lost; matching existing gh behavior does not resolve that upstream contract gap. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Provide concrete family schema types or explicitly amend sc2 to accept runtime-only family shapes; do not leave the contract decision solely as future work.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"A result that fails the output union is reported as rejected.","evidence":"The design describes output-union failure as rejected, but executeTool explicitly returns failed('schema-mismatch', ...) when result data fails validation. withGhFailureNet wraps execute only and cannot intercept this subsequent executor check. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Distinguish reader failures (rejected) from executor output-validation failures (schema-mismatch), and test both.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused shell and approval infrastructure supports bounded capture, closed stdin and denial before execution.","evidence":"runShellBytes uses stdin 'ignore' when no input is supplied, exposes truncation/overflow/timeout/abort fields and kills the process group. shouldAsk always asks for destructive calls; executeTool returns denied before tool.execute when approval is unavailable. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Retain the proposed capture checks and explicit no-client integration test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every s6 acceptance criterion has a corresponding proposed test.","evidence":"Compared DEF s6 ac1–ac6 with §7: coverage/registration, missing installation/sign-in, output validation, destructive approval, acli-only spawning and unsupported-operation inventory each have named tests. Scope exclusions still require the amendment noted above. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Retain the mapping and add the schema-mismatch case identified above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Project mutation success readers are supported by recorded real success output.","evidence":"The inventory explicitly states 'The success text of these five commands is not recorded yet'. The design supplies a gated probe as the acceptance prerequisite, but no recorded successful project-mutation fixtures are available to check. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Run the authorized disposable-project probe and retain its fixtures before accepting these readers, as the design requires.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":3,"low":9,"unverified":2},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T18:35:32.211Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
