9984	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s6","entry":{"id":"review-b08ec27002a4ee55966933c698dcd4af","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:20:53.452Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The five families cover s6's acceptance criteria subject to the explicitly proposed scope amendment.","evidence":"DEF §6.6 requires Jira operations, transitions, checked results, authentication failures, destructive approval, exclusive use of acli, and named unsupported operations. The recorded acli inventory supports the proposed families and status-name transitions. The scope-amendment table explicitly excludes create-bulk, file-based project forms, session changes, and unrelated domains; approval remains a prerequisite. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Obtain explicit approval of the scope amendment with the LLD before building against its reduced coverage.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing builder lacks maximum, maxItems, deduplication, and flag-value dash checks.","evidence":"fieldSchema emits integer 'minimum' and array 'minItems: 1'. buildArgv preserves supplied arrays. refuseInput's dash check selects only arguments containing 'pos' or 'spread', and only with dashSafe enabled. The complete relevant functions support Jira-owned bounds and normalization. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"Retain the proposed Jira-specific checks.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Jira tool implementation is additive, and the approval snapshot permits newly registered tools.","evidence":"Source search found Jira only in understanding identity/type declarations, with no acli implementation. registerBuiltinTools currently registers gh but no Jira domain. The snapshot test explicitly says 'Tools that later Stories add are not in the snapshot and are not compared' and iterates the old records rather than asserting the live registry size. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/__tests__/approval-class-mapping.test.ts, src/understanding/identity.ts, src/shared/understanding.ts]","action":"Add the registration call and new-tool assertions without changing the existing snapshot.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The exported gh builder primitives and failure wrapper support reuse without running gh.","evidence":"OpDef, OutSpec, argument constructors, refuseInput, buildArgv, schema builders, rejectInput and GhFamilyTool are exported. For custom outputs, buildArgv appends no gh JSON field list. withGhFailureNet only wraps tool.execute and preserves existing failures; it performs no CLI execution. GhFamilyTool is 'TypedTool & { readonly ops: readonly OpDef[] }'. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts]","action":"Use the primitives and wrapper as proposed, with Jira owning execution and answer construction.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding registerJiraTools to the existing builtin aggregator is sufficient to expose the new domain through daemon startup.","evidence":"registerBuiltinTools invokes each domain registration unconditionally, including registerGhTools. daemon/index.ts invokes registerBuiltinTools. The proposed addition follows the existing startup path without changing caller signatures. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/index.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"Add the Jira import and registration immediately after gh as specified.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed dependency relationship is adequately documented and its generated companion renders consistently.","evidence":"The HTML source contains four components and three directed arrows from Jira to op-table, helpers, and shell-helper, matching §3.4 and its ownership explanation. No persistent entity relationship or UX change requires an ERD or mock. Rendering was attempted with headless Chrome but failed with 'Failed to create a unique user data directory for headless' in the restricted environment; layout and rendered labels were not verified. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/component-dependency.html]","action":"Render the existing companion in a writable browser environment and inspect arrows, labels, and layout.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Runtime family typing matches current code, but relaxing the upstream typed-result guarantee requires the explicitly identified sc2 amendment.","evidence":"HLD sc2 promises results typed from the supplied definition; DEF s2 ac5 requires that type without a cast. Current GhFamilyTool exposes plain TSchema through TypedTool, and callTool derives Static from those schemas. The LLD accurately identifies this limitation and makes amendment approval an explicit dependency rather than silently changing s2 implementation. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, src/daemon/tools/call-tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/op-table.ts]","action":"File and approve the sc2 amendment before accepting runtime-only family typing as the shared contract.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Reader failures can remain rejected while successful answers with invalid or absent data become schema-mismatch outside the family wrapper.","evidence":"executeTool returns unsuccessful tool results directly, then checks successful results for missing data and output-schema mismatch. Both produce 'schema-mismatch'. withGhFailureNet wraps execute only and preserves an existing failure, so it cannot intercept the executor's subsequent validation. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/gh/helpers.ts]","action":"Keep both integration tests proposed in §7.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused process and approval infrastructure supports closed stdin, bounded capture, cancellation, and denial before execution.","evidence":"runShellBytes selects stdin 'ignore' when no input is supplied, reports stdoutTruncated, stderrOverflow, aborted and timedOut, and kills the process group. shouldAsk returns true unconditionally for destructive calls. executeTool returns a denied result before tool.execute when approval is absent or declined. [files: src/daemon/tools/shell-helper.ts, src/daemon/tools/approval-policy.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"Pass the proposed limits and signal through to runShellBytes and retain the no-client test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.3","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A success mark reliably identifies successful output for every project mutation.","evidence":"The recorded project mutation inventory explicitly states 'The success text of these five commands is not recorded yet'. Existing write-probe evidence covers work items, comments and links, not project mutations. The LLD acknowledges this gap and requires a disposable-project probe; no recorded project success output was available to validate its readers. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md]","action":"Complete the authorized disposable-project probe and capture each mutation's real output before accepting those readers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every s6 acceptance criterion has a proposed proving test aligned with the actual upstream requirement.","evidence":"Compared DEF §6.6 ac1–ac6 with §7: independent operation coverage proves ac1; install/sign-in and credential checks prove ac2; per-op output and executor validation tests prove ac3; destructive classification and denial prove ac4; spawn-only checks prove ac5; named unsupported operations prove ac6. The recorded exit-0 FAILURE batches and clone source-id behavior are specifically covered. These are design mappings, not executed Jira test results. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S006/LLD.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Implement the mapped tests and enforce the stated project-fixture acceptance gate even when optional live tests skip.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":11,"unverified":2},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-25T19:20:53.452Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
